            "description": "Watch Ivory Coast U20 vs Congo DR U20 highlights and goals from Friendly on ReFooty: Football Highlights Hub. Match played on June 13, 2026. The stage was set for a fascinating international clash on June 13, 2026 , as two talented sides faced off in a highly anticipated friendly. The atmosphere was electric with 33,636 fans in attendance, witnessing a match that would be decided by the finest of margins. First Half: French Dominance and Cherki’s Breakthrough From the opening whistle, France looked to impose their rhythm, controlling the ball and pinning Ivory Coast back. Early chances fell to Marcus Thuram , whose effort in the 9th minute missed the target, and Adrien Rabiot , who saw a powerful long-range strike fizz just wide of the post. The Ivorian defense, led by Yahia Fofana , remained under pressure as Aurelien Tchouameni forced a comfortable save with a header following a corner from Kylian Mbappé . Just as the first half seemed destined to end goalless, the deadlock was broken in the 45th minute. Ibrahima Konaté provided a perfectly weighted assist for Rayan Cherki , who found the back of the net with a precise right-footed finish. The tension boiled over shortly after, as Franck Kessie received a yellow card for dissent, leaving Ivory Coast trailing as they headed into the tunnel. Second Half: The Ivorian Resurgence The restart saw a flurry of substitutions from both managers. France introduced several fresh faces, including N'Golo Kanté and Lucas Digne , while Ivory Coast brought on Amad Diallo and Nicolas Pépé . The changes had an immediate impact. In the 53rd minute, Nicolas Pépé turned provider, setting up Guela Doué , who clinically equalized with his right foot to breathe new life into the contest. The middle period of the second half was defined by tactical adjustments and offside calls as both teams searched for a winning edge. France continued to threaten through corners from Maghnes Akliouche , but the Ivorian backline, bolstered by the introduction of Ousmane Diomandé , stood firm against the pressure. Late Drama and Diallo’s Decisive Strike The match reached its climax in the 84th minute. Guela Doué , already a scorer, turned creator by delivering a crucial ball to Amad Diallo . The substitute made no mistake, firing home with his right foot to complete the turnaround for Ivory Coast . Despite five minutes of added time and desperate late attempts by France , including dangerous crosses from Lucas Digne , the Ivorian defense held their ground. Emmanuel Agbadou provided a vital late clearance to secure the victory. As the final whistle blew, the scoreboard reflected a hard-fought battle where the Ivory Coast clinical finishing proved to be the difference.",
